From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:56:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: export a locked, acknowledged
 update of one power request bit

The PS-REQ word of the PMP report is shared by every client of the PMP:
the report entries (display, ISP, video decode, the AFNC IOAs), the T6001
AGX vote (bit 9) and, out of tree, the ANE clock level of omarchy-ane
(bit 10). The report entries and the AGX vote read-modify-write the word
under rep->lock. A module outside this driver could only map the window
and read-modify-write it without that lock, so a concurrent write of
another bit could be lost.

apple_pmp_report_set_request(report_np, id, enable, no_ack) is the one
writer a client outside this file may use. It calls the same
apple_pmp_report_set_state() the entries use, so it takes the same lock
and does the same acknowledge poll (at most 50 ms). The caller owns the
bit it asks for.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit f7ad8cffcacb77bcba84adbfb67965e8ea865bb0)
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c  | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h | 12 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index e29dce40b8..56eb082909 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -1542,6 +1542,49 @@ int apple_pmp_report_set_t6030_gfx(struct device *supplier, bool enable)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_report_set_t6030_gfx);
 
+/**
+ * apple_pmp_report_set_request() - set or clear one bit of the PMP power request word of a bound report
+ * @report_np: device tree node of the report region (compatible apple,t6000-pmp-v2-report and its
+ *	siblings)
+ * @id: bit number of the request, the index of the soc-device record, 0 to 63 (ANE0 is 10 and AGX
+ *	is 9 on the T6001)
+ * @enable: set or clear the bit
+ * @no_ack: do not wait for the acknowledge
+ *
+ * One read-modify-write of the word, made under the report's lock: the same lock every report
+ * entry and the AGX vote take, so requests for different bits cannot lose each other. Unless
+ * @no_ack, waits (atomic poll, at most 50 ms) until the acknowledge word shows the bit as
+ * requested. A PMP that does not run has nothing to acknowledge: the request is written and 0 is
+ * returned, as for a report entry.
+ *
+ * The caller owns the bit it requests; this function does not arbitrate between callers of the
+ * same bit. On the T6001 bit 9 belongs to the AGX vote (pmp_report.agx_vote), so other callers
+ * must not use it.
+ *
+ * Context: process context (the acknowledge wait is a busy poll of up to 50 ms).
+ * Return: 0, -ENODEV if no report is bound to @report_np, -EINVAL if @id is out of range,
+ * -ETIMEDOUT if the acknowledge did not follow.
+ */
+int apple_pmp_report_set_request(const struct device_node *report_np, unsigned int id,
+				bool enable, bool no_ack)
+{
+	struct apple_pmp_report *rep;
+	int ret = -ENODEV;
+
+	if (id > 63)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	list_for_each_entry_rcu(rep, &apple_pmp_reports, list) {
+		if (rep->dev->of_node == report_np) {
+			ret = apple_pmp_report_set_state(rep, id, enable, no_ack);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_report_set_request);
+
 static int apple_pmp_report_entry_set_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, bool enable)
 {
 	struct apple_pmp_report_entry *ent = genpd_to_apple_pmp_report_entry(genpd);
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
index 7fb5327a7b..345848c91d 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@ int apple_pmp_report_set_t6030_gfx(struct device *supplier, bool enable);
 int apple_pmp_report_wait_ready(struct device_node *entry, unsigned long timeout);
 int apple_pmp_report_fast_die_effort(const struct device_node *np,
 				     unsigned int lane, u8 *effort);
+/*
+ * Set or clear one bit of the PMP power request word of the report bound to @report_np, under the
+ * report's lock, with the acknowledge wait (see pmp-report.c).
+ */
+int apple_pmp_report_set_request(const struct device_node *report_np, unsigned int id,
+				 bool enable, bool no_ack);
 /*
  * T6001: the GPU driver reports each operation in flight. With the pmp_report.agx_vote parameter set, the AGX request (PS-REQ bit 9) is
  * set while any operation runs and cleared agx_vote_idle_ms after the last one ends. Parameter off: no effect. Both may be called from
@@ -69,6 +75,12 @@ static inline int apple_pmp_report_fast_die_effort(const struct device_node *np,
 {
 	return -ENODEV;
 }
+
+static inline int apple_pmp_report_set_request(const struct device_node *report_np,
+					       unsigned int id, bool enable, bool no_ack)
+{
+	return -ENODEV;
+}
 #endif
 
 #endif /* _LINUX_SOC_APPLE_PMP_REPORT_H_ */
